NOTE ON LICENSE CHOICE

This project uses a restrictive, all-rights-reserved license rather than a permissive
open-source license (such as MIT or Apache 2.0) because the author has indicated an
intention to keep the implementation proprietary, potentially for future intellectual
property evaluation (see IP_DOCUMENTATION.md and ORIGINALITY.md).

Choosing a restrictive license means:
- Others cannot legally copy, modify, or redistribute the code without permission.
- This preserves the author's ability to later pursue IP protection, commercialization,
  or exclusive licensing, since the work has not been made freely available to the public.
- The tradeoff is reduced visibility/collaboration compared to an open-source license —
  this is a deliberate choice, not an oversight.

If the author later decides to open-source part or all of the project, this LICENSE file
should be replaced with the appropriate open-source license text (e.g., MIT, Apache-2.0)
and the copyright header should be updated accordingly.

This is an academic project. No warranty of any kind is provided. The author is not liable
for any damages arising from the use of this software.
